* Greatest Common Divisor — Knuth Vol.1, Algorithm E (Euclid's algorithm)
* Computes GCD of values at addresses M and N, stores result at GCD
*
* rI1 = u, rI2 = v (or rA/rX)
M       EQU     1000        * address of first number
N       EQU     1001        * address of second number
R       EQU     1002        * address for result
        ORIG    M
        CON     252         * first number
        CON     105         * second number
        CON     0           * result placeholder
        ORIG    3000
START   ENTA    0
        LDA     M           * rA = u
        LDX     N           * rX = v
E1      CMPX    =0=         * v = 0?
        JE      DONE
E2      STX     T           * t = v
        DIV     N           * rA = u/v, rX = u mod v
        CMPA    =0=
        JE      E3
        LDX     T           * rX = t (= old v)
        STX     N
        LDA     T
        JMP     E1
E3      LDX     T
        STX     N
        LDA     T
        JMP     E1
DONE    STX     R           * result in rX
        HLT
T       CON     0           * temp
        END     START
